# Screen 06 · Crest the Rinse Arch

**Candidate for the bent washer passage and clearer steering views. The owner’s visual approval is pending.** Claudia’s playable version is the baseline. The full Screen 06 composition still needs work after the initial crest.

## What Benny swims through

The original shows a broad cyan crest curling around a patch of purple slotted metal, with a chain of gold coins leading toward a gold-ringed passage on the right. Claudia’s deep view turns into a tightly packed gold bullseye. On the experimental ride you can follow the cyan river through more widely separated collars and around the right-hand bend. The white foam sits beyond the steering line, exposing more of Benny’s lower body when he leans. At the exit the gold collar and slotted outer wall still occupy different depths as the camera passes them.

The left curl now has a raised shoulder, a rounded lip and a visible underside. Swept metal panels seat the outside returns against the washer drum. The near river uses shorter highlights measured along its own curved surface. Its native art swatch was previously stretched across five times its sampled length. The moving water still repeats some bright strokes. The purple metal looks flatter and the foam thinner than the original artwork at several moving angles.

The purple opening beneath the crest remains the most important unfinished landmark. It is visible at the approved opening and near crest release. By +3 game units, the near water covers much of it and photographic detail smears on the right shoulder. This proof improves the surroundings and the deeper passage. It falls short of reconstructing the negative space around the entire swimming path. The warm, broad depth of the original washer and the thickness of all its hidden rings still need owner review.

## The measured opening

Both captures and the original are native 864 × 1536. Per pixel we compute the mean absolute difference of red, green and blue on a 0–255 scale. Claudia has **79.09%** of pixels within 20 levels. The candidate has **79.10%**. The 265 × 135 area inside the crest opening is **92.53%** on both. The separate gold-and-wall region goes from **98.63% to 98.77%**. The native whole-frame result is essentially level with Claudia’s. The moving views have no matching approved pictures or similarity percentages. [Measured regions](checks/opening-regions.json) · [Independent Pixelmatch and matching camera checks](checks/motion.json)

The approved image’s score reads 1,680. The game’s deep capture reads 1,580 under the deterministic sampling route. Each experimental game image uses the same score, HUD, actor, camera, lights, shader clock, input and station as its Claudia counterpart. An independent capture of Claudia’s opening reproduced every pixel.

