## Gameplay and viewing times

Both real Three.js films run continuously from inlet to exit with identical inputs. The game simulates at 60 steps per second. Each H.264 film samples 63 frames at 12 fps, 648 × 1152. The 14 native still pairs include +3, +6, +10, +20, hard left and right, inlet, middle, deep, crest release, the last frame inside the stage, and the following transition. All eight gameplay assertions passed. A complete safe ride collected 91 coins, moved the score from 1,330 to 2,240 and reached Stage 11 with five hearts and zero collisions. [Both films and separate pictures](PHONE_REVIEW.md)

The film’s first part enters the crest. Inspect the upper water and the right shoulder as the camera changes angle. Then follow the open lanes between the rings and where the foam touches the side of the water. The stage switches from 06 into 07 at **4.92 seconds**. The exact frame-by-frame stations, steering, camera and shader clocks are recorded alongside each clip. [Retained timeline](CLAUDIA_BEFORE/route.json) · [Candidate timeline](CODEX_NEW/route.json)

